# Idea loop: Mapping AAV capsid-receptor interactions to explain barrier transcytosis versus intracellular retention

Root question: Can molecular mapping of AAV capsid-receptor interactions on brain microvascular endothelial cells determine which AAV variants transcytose across the blood-brain barrier versus remain intracellular, and for which capsid-receptor binding signatures?

Expanded from a one-line seed (framer: NOT COMPUTE-BOUND): option Structural coverage of capsid–receptor–glycan complexes "Structural coverage of capsid–receptor–glycan complexes", the strongest of 4 the widener listed that the screen labelled SAME.

## Screen (option-critic panel, medians)

| Option | stakes | open | reshape | total | changes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| O Structural coverage of capsid–receptor–glycan complexes | 5 | 5 | 3 | 10 |  |
| V1 Full glycosylated capsid–receptor–glycan complexes instead of peptide fragments | 5 | 3 | 3 | 8 | Changes the system studied from peptide–receptor-domain fragments in water to full glycosylated capsid–receptor–glycan complexes, closing the gap that GPI-anchored ALPL, glycosylated LRP6, CA-IV and the 60-mer capsid context are absent; it also makes the result directly relevant to Voyager's ALPL-NeuroShuttle and the Gradinaru lab's LRP6 mapping. |
| V2 Cell-level Transwell transcytosis as the comparison | 5 | 1 | 3 | 6 | Changes the comparison it is judged against from self-defined 10-ns contact labels and 320-ns runs to cell-level Transwell transcytosis plus receptor knockout, closing the gap that no programme has a computed classifier validated against cell-level transcytosis; aimed at Voyager's TRACER platform and the Gradinaru lab. |
| V3 Millisecond pH-resolved off-rates and release probabilities, not ten-ns contact survival | 5 | 5 | 3 | 10 | Changes the quantity more compute buys from ten-ns contact-survival proxies to pH-resolved off-rates and endosomal-release probabilities with error bars at 5,000 parallel simulations per iteration, closing the gap that ten-ns proxies are not the millisecond-scale off-rates or release steps that determine transcytosis. |

No variant scored higher than the original; no second card.

## Rounds

**r0:** card PASS 2/2, critic sum 21/25 (lever 3, open 5, stakes 3, verifiable 5, internals —, reshape 5, baseline 5), $946 at p_score · plan $946 · 2 GUESS. Frame: Voyager Therapeutics — TRACER capsid discovery platform / NeuroShuttle, fit 3, change 3, new 5 (11/15).

